Implement user story SKY-002-test: Write vitest test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests covering all SkyscannerClient behaviors: URL/header construction, successful parsing, HTTP errors, missing API key, malformed responses, and mock mode verification. All tests mock global fetch — no real network calls.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts contains at least 5 vitest tests using mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) with afterEach fetch restoration
- Tests cover: correct RapidAPI URL and header construction; successful response parsed into FlightResult[]; HTTP 4xx rejection with status code in error message; missing API key constructor error; malformed/missing-fields response body rejects with parse/validation error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' mode: fetch spy is never invoked and deterministic fixture FlightResult[] is returned
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API with non-'true' values (unset, empty string, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') still performs real fetch call — strict opt-in, not fuzzy truthy
- Test verifies real failures (4xx, 5xx, network error, malformed body) are never silently replaced with mock/fixture data
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class SkyscannerClient is exported from /home/bradleyjerome/projects/skyscanner-app/src/skyscanner/client.ts
- Constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'SkyscannerClient: missing API key. Provide apiKey to the constructor or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when no API key provided
- Constructor resolves API key from constructor param first, then RAPIDAPI_KEY env var
- Method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- Mock mode activates only when process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string equality, case-sensitive)
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', searchFlights returns mockFixture(params) without calling fetch
- mockFixture returns array of 3 FlightResult objects with deterministic values based on params seed
- Real API endpoint: POST https://${SKYSCANNER_API_HOST}/v1/flights/search (default host: skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com)
- Request headers include: 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-RapidAPI-Key': this.#apiKey, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': SKYSCANNER_HOST
- Request body JSON: { origin, destination, date, adults: params.adults ?? 1 }
- Network errors throw Error with message: 'SkyscannerClient: network error while calling Skyscanner API: ${original}'
- HTTP 4xx/5xx errors throw Error with message: 'SkyscannerClient: Skyscanner API request failed with status ${status} ${statusText}'
- JSON parse errors throw Error with message: 'SkyscannerClient: failed to parse Skyscanner API response as JSON: ${original}'
- Response body parsed from: body.flights, body.results, body.data, or top-level array
- Malformed response (non-array) throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: malformed response from Skyscanner API: expected an array of flights at body.flights or top-level array'
- Each flight entry validated for: price (number), currency (non-empty string), airline (non-empty string), departure (non-empty string), arrival (non-empty string), duration (number), stops (number)
- Validation error format: 'SkyscannerClient: malformed response entry at index ${index}: missing or invalid fields: ${fieldList}'
- No validation on adults lower bound - adults=0 is accepted
- No validation on date format - any string accepted
- No validation on origin/destination format - any non-empty string accepted

